  "text": "Allergies:\ncephalexin / fluoxetine / Macrolide Antibiotics / ofloxacin / \nranitidine\n\nChief Complaint:\ncolonoscopy prep\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ female with history of\nT2DM, asthma, HTN, and ___ hereditary osteopdystrophy who\npresents for planned extended colonoscopy prep after failed\noutpatient prep x2. \n\nPatient underwent routine colonoscopy in ___ of this year \nbut\ndue to poor prep had to repeat this in ___. In ___ she\nunderwent colonoscopy with transverse colon polypectomy but \nagain\nhad prepped poorly and decision made to plan for inpatient\nextended colonoscopy prep with clear liquids and 2 day prep with\nNulyteley per GI. Poor preps have been attributed to\nnoncompliance with clear liquid diet prior to ___. Of note,\nmother with history of colon cancer.\n\nOn arrival to the floor patient is without acute complaints. \n\nROS: Pertinent positives and negatives as noted in the HPI.  All\nother systems were reviewed and are negative.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nPt was admitted for colonoscopy prep over two days given \nmultiple failed preps at home.   Pt was prepped slowly over 2 \ndays and tolerated it well.  Pt was clear by ___ afternoon \nand was very eager to advance her diet.  Pt was redirected to \nremain NPO after midnight and was taken for colonoscopy without \nincident on ___.   Pt was advanced a diet without difficulty \nand was discharged home to care of family on ___.    There were \nno changes made to her home medication regimen.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nAnemia\nColonoscopy",
